    "notes":  "**A rule with no entry condition could sit there saying \"Running\" all session.** It went on, the screen said Running, and the trade list said \"no trades yet, the conditions in your rule have not happened\". They had not happened because there were none. The Backtest gate checked for this; the Start-live-test button skips the backtest on purpose - for anyone whose broker serves no history - and skipped the check with it. One guard now covers every way a rule can be switched on, and it tells you what to fix rather than just refusing.",
